    "language": [],
    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "EdTrust—West (ETW) aims to eliminate educational disparities in California by collaborating with schools, conducting research, and advocating for equitable policies. The Educator Engagement (EE) Team conducts Systemic Equity Reviews (SERs) in districts and higher education institutions, serving as a crucial liaison between ETW and local school communities.\r\n\r\nPreviously, ETW relied on informal methods to integrate SER findings into its activities. This project establishes a formal, recurring process to incorporate EE insights into ETW’s broader work, prioritizing the voices of educators, students, and school leaders.\r\n\r\nThe outcomes of this project include the development of Knowledge Integration Tool (KIT) Prototypes and Final KITs, a Creation Guide for the EE team, a User Guide for non-EE teams, and a Final Report linking these deliverables together.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
